Below is a quick‑reference list of the **long‑weekend periods** that arise from Canada’s federal holidays in 2023.  
(If you need province‑specific holidays that also create long weekends—e.g. Family Day in Alberta, British Columbia, Saskatchewan, etc.—just let me know and I can add those too.)

| Long‑Weekend Period | Holiday(s) Involved | Observed Dates (2023) | Notes |
|---------------------|---------------------|-----------------------|-------|
| **Jan 1 – 3** | New Year’s Day (observed Mon Jan 2) | 2023‑01‑01 (Sun) – 2023‑01‑03 (Tue) | New Year’s Day falls on Sunday → observed Monday. |
| **Feb 18 – 20** | Family Day (in Alberta, BC, Saskatchewan, etc.) | 2023‑02‑18 (Sat) – 2023‑02‑20 (Mon) | Only provinces that observe Family Day get this long weekend. |
| **Apr 7 – 9** | Good Friday | 2023‑04‑07 (Fri) – 2023‑04‑09 (Sun) | Good Friday is a federal holiday; the weekend follows. |
| **May 20 – 22** | Victoria Day | 2023‑05‑20 (Sat) – 2023‑05‑22 (Mon) | Victoria Day is always the Monday before May 25. |
| **Jul 1 – 3** | Canada Day (observed Mon Jul 3) | 2023‑07‑01 (Sat) – 2023‑07‑03 (Mon) | Canada Day falls on Saturday → observed Monday. |
| **Sep 2 – 4** | Labour Day | 2023‑09‑02 (Sat) – 2023‑09‑04 (Mon) | Labour Day is always the first Monday in September. |
| **Oct 7 – 9** | Thanksgiving | 2023‑10‑07 (Sat) – 2023‑10‑09 (Mon) | Thanksgiving is always the second Monday in October. |
| **Nov 11 – 13** | Remembrance Day (observed Mon Nov 13) | 2023‑11‑11 (Sat) – 2023‑11‑13 (Mon) | Remembrance Day falls on Saturday → observed Monday. |
| **Dec 23 – 25** | Christmas | 2023‑12‑23 (Sat) – 2023‑12‑25 (Mon) | Christmas is always on Monday in 2023. |

